cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fine-crack-tracing: crack segmentation masks to measured centrelines"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rami
    family-names: Kronbi
    website: "https://ramikronbi.com"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kronbii/fine-crack-tracing"
url: "https://ramikronbi.com/projects/fine-crack-tracing-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A Python package and command-line tool that turns crack segmentation masks
  into measured centrelines. Each crack is skeletonised and read as a graph,
  spurs are pruned against the crack's width, breaks are bridged, and the width
  across the crack is measured at every point to sub-pixel, with a Shi-Tomasi
  corner tracer as the fallback. Includes a synthetic benchmark with exact
  ground truth.
keywords:
  - crack detection
  - crack width
  - skeletonization
  - centerline extraction
  - infrastructure inspection
  - computer vision
